text:
Maya: FYI hitting a soft cap on private deployment GPUs in eu-west-1 for tenant acme-corp — autoscaler refusing new allocations, queueing started :warning:
ops-bot: [alert] cluster-euw1-gpu pool at 96% alloc, queue_length=42, avg_wait=3.2s https://grafana/redwood/cluster-euw1
Sam: Ugh. Is this the reserved headroom policy kicking in or actual physical scarcity?
Maya: Physical. We exhausted the node quota because a long-running job pinned 4x A100s. Autoscaler kept minimal headroom but can't add nodes due to AZ capacity.
Leo: Quick question — do we want to tell customers to throttle on their side or we take longer-term action?
Anya: Both. Immediate: surface a clear 429 + Retry-After + queue-position headers so clients can back off gracefully. Medium: advise them on client-side concurrency controls and recommend burst credits / Dedicated if sustained.
Sam: Can we agree on header contract? I propose: `Retry-After`, `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-Queue-Position`, `X-Estimated-Wait`
Maya: +1. Also include `Retry-After` seconds and an optional `X-Fallback-Model: smaller-model` when we can automatically suggest a cheaper model.
infra-sre: we'll emit 429s once node_util > 90% and queue_len > 20. Config draft: `reject_threshold: 0.9`, `queue_max: 200`, `headroom_reserve: 0.1`
Sam: For customer guidance, what client patterns do we recommend?
Anya: Short list: 1) Limit concurrent requests per API key (recommended range 6-12 depending on model). 2) Exponential backoff with full jitter. 3) Accept stream fallback or lower max_tokens for high latency. 4) Respect `Retry-After` and `X-Queue-Position` to implement local queueing.
Maya: Add a formula suggestion for concurrency: `concurrency_per_gpu ~= floor(gpu_mem_gb / 24) * 2` (empirical; e.g., A100-80 -> ~6-8). Put clear note: adjust for sequence length.
Leo: Can we provide a JS snippet for retries for customers?
Anya: Yep. Example (short):
```js
async function callWithRetry(fn){
  let delay = 100;
  for(let i=0;i<6;i++){
    const res = await fn();
    if(res.status === 429){
      const ra = parseInt(res.headers.get('Retry-After') || '0');
      const jitter = Math.floor(Math.random() * delay);
      const wait = Math.max(ra*1000, delay + jitter);
      await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, wait));
      delay = Math.min(delay*2, 2000);
      continue;
    }
    return res;
  }
  throw new Error('exhausted retries');
}
```
Maya: Also recommend clients expose a circuit-breaker: if 5 consecutive 5xx/429 within 60s then pause for 30s.
infra-sre: On our side, we should publish a small KB with: recommended headers, concurrency table per GPU type, example config for nginx/ingress rate limiting, and a sample client policy file.
Sam: What about queue visibility? Customers ask why their requests are "stuck".
Maya: We'll return `X-Queue-Position: 12` and `X-Estimated-Wait: 2.8s` in the 429 body and also log a trace id so support can correlate. Example response:
```http
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 3
X-RateLimit-Limit: 100
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0
X-Queue-Position: 12
X-Estimated-Wait: 2.8
Content-Type: application/json

{"error":"capacity_exceeded","trace_id":"tr_abc123","message":"Cluster capacity exceeded — reduce concurrency or retry after indicated time."}
```
Leo: Nice. Also add guidance: if customers need predictable throughput, recommend Dedicated or increase private cluster node quota.
Anya: Cost note to include: throttling reduces cost but increases tail latency — we should show trade-offs: e.g., 10% lower cost with 20% higher P95 if you switch to smaller model + batching.
Maya: Action items: infra-sre will push header + 429 behavior behind feature flag today. I'll draft customer KB and sample nginx config. Sam, can you prepare an email template for CSMs explaining temporary throttling behavior and recommended client changes?
Sam: Yep, I’ll draft and share by EOD.
ops-bot: [note] feature-flag db updated: `emit_capacity_429=true`
Maya: Thanks — I'll update the private deploy runbook to include the concurrency formula and JS snippet.
Anya: I'll add a short section in the Public KB about admission control, plus a recommended `Retry-After` policy matrix for different models.
Maya: Closing loop — we'll monitor queue_len and avg_wait in the next 24h and consider granting a one-time quota bump if acme-corp needs a scheduled migration.
Sam: Sounds good. :thumbsup:
